# FAST GUNS — environment template
# ============================================================================
# Copy to .env.local for development. For production set EVERY variable below
# in Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables. There are NO defaults: the
# server refuses to boot (fails closed) without all three secrets, and values
# matching historical/burned credentials are rejected everywhere.
#
# Generate strong values:
#   openssl rand -base64 24        (gate + boss key)
#   openssl rand -hex 32           (attestation secret)
# ============================================================================

# Front-door passphrase — HIGH ENTROPY required (min 16 chars in production).
# This is the only shared credential. It also seeds the WANTED-board content
# key client-side (PBKDF2-SHA512, 600k iterations). The old 3-digit public
# code is retired and its value is on the burned list.
GATE_PASSCODE=""

# Boss key for the reserved DRACH callsign (min 16 chars in production).
# Verified server-side in constant time; never stored, never logged.
DRACH_KEY=""

# HMAC secret for callsign attestations + capability tokens (min 32 chars in
# production). The root of administrative authorization — treat accordingly.
FAST_ATTEST_SECRET=""

# OPTIONAL distributed rate-limiting backend (spec §7). When both are set the
# limiter becomes cluster-wide (keys are HMAC digests — raw IPs never leave
# the app) and backend errors fail CLOSED. Leave unset for instance-local
# limiting.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=""
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=""
